uYCMxNDNg&&bt=890&ft=arR-Iqq2m0nPD12LAPEI3wUtsI8AMeF~O5&mime_type=video_mp4&rc=O2RnZTplNDU7ODZlPGRoZUBpank2eG85cjgzeTMzZzczNEBhLjU0NGIuXl4xLi9eNi4tYSNeal5iMmQ0ZW5gLS1kMS9zcw%3D%3D&vvpl=1&l=2026110616200299FC2CEF35952D15876F&btag=e00098000"}},{"id":"7647991347810536734","caption":"🚨 FREE Recruiting Workshop Alert! 🚨 If you’re a parent of a student-athlete, this is one workshop you don’t want to miss. The recruiting process can be confusing. Many families wait until high school to start learning about recruiting, only to realize they are already behind. The truth is that recruiting begins long before college coaches start making offers. It starts with building good habits, maintaining strong grades, creating a recruiting profile, gathering film, and understanding what coaches are actually looking for. This free NCSA workshop, “Understanding Recruiting Standards,” will help athletes and parents learn: ✅ What college coaches look for when evaluating athletes ✅ How recruiting standards vary by division and school level ✅ When athletes should begin contacting coaches ✅ The importance of academics in the recruiting process ✅ How to build an effective recruiting profile ✅ What realistic expectations look like for student-athletes ✅ Steps families can take today to improve recruiting opportunities Whether your athlete is in middle school, high school, or just beginning their recruiting journey, gaining knowledge now can save time, money, and frustration later. Parents, one of the biggest mistakes I see is waiting until junior or senior year to start learning about recruiting. The families who educate themselves early often have more options and a clearer path through the process. 📅 Date: June 9, 2026 ⏰ Time: 7:00 PM Central Time Take advantage of this free opportunity to learn directly from recruiting experts and get answers to questions that many families have about the college recruiting process. Knowledge is power, and in recruiting, information can make all the differenc